  "title": "The Database Stack Has Changed. Why Are We Still Using Database Tools Built for 2010?",
  "summary": "Most engineering teams don’t rely on a single database anymore. Modern stacks are a mix of specialized systems: Postgres for transactions, Redis for caching, Elasticsearch for search, Neo4j for relationships, object storage for files, and vector databases for AI. The hard part is managing them all.",
